 "version": 1,
 "title": "Glass Bell Lead",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: the glassy, chiming digital bell of mid-80s FM synthesizers: a bright, crystalline strike that mellows as it rings.\n\nHow it's built: FM synthesis. A modulator sine (an octave and a sixth above the note) shakes the carrier sine's frequency (LIN FM). The modulator goes through its own VCA with a decaying envelope, so the brightness fades as the note rings, the way a struck bell's does. A second envelope shapes the volume; Chorus and Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: melodies and chords, in the middle and upper keys.\n\nTweak: the modulator's TUNE (whole octaves are pure, other values more bell-like or clangy), the carrier's LIN FM (brightness), the brightness envelope's DECAY.",
